---
import PolicyPage from "@/components/layout/PolicyPage.astro";
import { updateManifest } from "@/data/policies";
import { site } from "@/data/site";
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Muelle collects no data. The only network request is an update check in Settings, which you can turn off."
  updated="November 15, 2026"
>
  <p>Muelle has no accounts, no analytics and no telemetry. It does not collect, store or send personal data.</p>

  <h2>The one network request</h2>
  <p>
    When you open Settings, it asks GitHub whether a newer version exists, by downloading{" "}
    <code>{updateManifest}</code>. Nothing about you or your computer is sent with it; GitHub, like any website,
    sees your IP address and handles it under the{" "}
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub privacy statement</a>.
    If you choose to update, the installer is downloaded from the same GitHub releases page.
  </p>
  <p>
    To turn this off: Settings → System → <b>Check for updates automatically</b>. You can still check by hand with the
    Check button. The dock itself never connects to the network.
  </p>

  <h2>What stays on your computer</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>%APPDATA%\Muelle\config.json</code>: your settings and the apps you pinned.</li>
    <li><code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Muelle</code>: a cache of app icons and names, so the dock starts fast.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To read what is on screen (open windows, their icons, network and volume status for the menu bar), Muelle uses
    Windows itself; none of it leaves your computer. Uninstalling removes the cache, and optionally your settings.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Vercel and uses no cookies, analytics or trackers. Vercel may keep standard server logs
    (such as IP addresses) under the{" "}
    <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel privacy policy</a>.
    Downloads come from <a href={site.releases} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Releases</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={site.issues} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open an issue on GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
